---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & license"
  description={`Who runs ${site.name}, how content is sourced and reviewed, licenses, and what the analytics collect.`}
  editPath="src/pages/about.astro"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>About &amp; license</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        {site.name} is an open-source, community-maintained reference that keeps every Sondors
        Metacycle on the road: what each part is, where to buy it today, and how to fix the common
        failures. Sondors went out of business, so owners depend on each other for parts and service
        knowledge.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every fact should have a source and a date. Content lives as plain files in a{' '}
        <a href={site.repoUrl}>GitHub repository</a> so anyone can fork it. {site.editor} is the
        editor and reviews every change.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site builds on the community's existing work, especially{' '}
        <a href="https://metacyclopedia.github.io/">Metacyclopedia</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        No accounts and no ads, and this site sets no cookies. Your theme choice and guide
        checkboxes are saved only in your own browser. The web form's spam check (Cloudflare
        Turnstile) runs only on the form page.{' '}
        {site.analytics
          ? `Page views are counted with ${site.analytics.provider}, which is cookieless and stores no personal data.`
          : 'No analytics.'}{' '}
        See the <a href="/disclaimer#analytics">Disclaimer</a> for exactly what's collected. The web
        form's optional name or handle is published with your report, so leave it blank if you'd
        rather not be credited.
      </p>

      <h2>License</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Content (parts data, guides, troubleshooting):{' '}
          <a href={site.license.content.url}>{site.license.content.name}</a>. Reuse and adapt it;
          changes stay open.
        </li>
        <li>
          Code: <a href={site.license.code.url}>{site.license.code.name}</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Third-party material (manuals, diagrams, photos) keeps its original rights; see the{' '}
          <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
